														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2704789">
									

<p>There are a lot of parts to this and I think the density of the technical jargon takes away from an average reader's ability to understand article, but I think I was able to muddle through enough to give this a +1. All the technical detail does feel like the crux of the article, after all. It just feels a bit like a chore to get through in places. Also I'm a little surprised the documentation doesn't explicitly say that -B areas are like human blood vessels and -D areas are like human stomachs.</p>
<p>Another thing that stuck out to me is that this anomaly was apparently first discovered by the Foundation, while they were looking for somewhere to build their research site for microbiological anomalies, and the first known linked individual was a Foundation employee. That's&#8230; one hell of a coincidence (provided there isn't some cleverly-hinted reason as to why this might be that I missed). Still, this is fiction, so my +1 stays. Well done.</p>

							</div>

								
					
