														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2704802">
									

<p>I appreciate the feed back, in regards to B and D, I thought I had included statements correlating to what you've said. Guess I didn't, I'll see if I can fix the wording there to indicate as much. As far as the Technical Jargon goes, it continues to surprise me what is and is not considered Jargon, which varies based from person to person. The text is a bit dense and long, I agree, but as far as Jargon, in comparison to the the previous drafts, it is quite trimmed.</p>
<p>So the linked individual being a foundation employee was, honestly, on my part completely intentional, same goes for the discovery. There's no clear indicator as to why it happens like this in-universe, I thought about making a more clear connection, however after some debate I decided it would be better to leave the reader thinking about what might be really going on here, if whatever is behind the anomaly <em>knows</em> about the foundation, and is guiding them in some manner.</p>
<p>It's also important to remember that full sequencing of the human genome didn't occur until 2003, however since foundation techniques and technology is usually at least a decade ahead of the general public they were able to employ it early. An increase in Class 1 events lead to concern that something might happen, and so they employed this novel technique to try and see if something was happening on a genetic level. What did they find? That this thing was genetically identical to one of their operatives, an operative, who, worked around the entity and was recently diagnosed with Colon cancer.</p>

							</div>

								
					
