<p>I wasn't really enamored of &quot;microscopic structures but larger&quot; as a trick the first time it was deployed, and seeing it again so soon isn't really helping that.</p>
<p>I held off on commenting on the first iteration of this, because while I don't really like articles that lean heavily on technical precepts and things like violating the Square Cube Law, I can see that there's probably a place for that sort of thing. But seeing the same general concept, executed in largely the same way, now we're at a point where it feels like a formula being milked for all its worth, and I'd rather not see repeated exercises in the same thing.</p>
<p>I mean, it's refreshing to see articles that don't get their length from overly narmy interview logs or fifteen collapsibles about how the real document is in the next castle, but between these two articles and the prion one earlier this week, this is a trend that I don't really want to see either.</p>

