			<div class="content" id="post-content-2704847">
									

<p>I appreciate your feedback Kalinin, and want to lay your fears to rest in regards to &quot;A formula being milked&quot;. I am moving away from the &quot;Giant microbe is giant and defies normal biophysical concepts&quot; and focusing more on the story the SCP has to tell, and what impacts their individual anomalous effects have. I focused more heavily on the square cube law and technical aspects in this and the previous article primarily because that's what I'm used to writing, and to establish myself on site with such high standards it became apparent that I would need to stick to my strengths and work on developing my narrative ability within clinical tone. From this point moving forward I will be attempting to balance narrative against detail, in a different manner from what you've seen so far to avoid the repetition and similarity you see between the two current pieces.</p>
<p>It's unfortunate that you mention the Prion article, as it's pretty clear from the writing that that particular piece was trying to play off the relative success of 2946. I critiqued that piece before it was posted, and attempted to guide the writer into a different direction from where I had tread, as well as correct his incorrect scientific assumptions. It's even more unfortunate that he only half listened to my critique, and left many of the issues I first pointed out unattended, while adding an exacerbated experiment log that was verbatim a direct copy of 2946's format.</p>
<p>Again, I reassure you that this won't become a formula from which to milk upvotes.</p>

