<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Nitpicking</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">I&nbsp;have&nbsp;hawk&nbsp;eyes&nbsp;for&nbsp;weird&nbsp;phrasing&nbsp;and&nbsp;science</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Just a forewarning some of this is just like, my opinion, man. I tend to phrase things in very deliberate ways when writing to help the flow, so feel free to disregard semantics-related bits unless you wanna go for it.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Personnel are to avoid physical interaction with SCP-2378-4 iterations at all costs.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I would rearrange this to be &quot;Physical interaction with SCP-2378-4 should(must?) be avoided by personnel at all costs.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Entry into SCP-2378-D is restricted to aerial corrosion-proof drones.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>What kind of material would be needed for this? Maybe put a footnote with recommended materials.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Personnel should avoid irritation of interior elements of SCP-2378.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Another bit I'd rearrange; &quot;Irritation to the interior element of SCP-2378 should be avoided.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Each of these organisms is capable of sensing large concentrations of sugar, even in a human host, and will engage in aggressive predatory behavior to secure these sources.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This sentence is definitely kind of wonky to me. Maybe &quot;These organisms have specialized sensory organelles for detecting significant accumulations of sugars (all sugar? or just glucose? or what?). They have predated on humans to collect the sugar content within them.&quot; Although the last bit of mine is also pretty weird. Maybe footnote it? Also, what do they do with the rest of the human body bits?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>viscous maroon or dark-blue/purple colored fluid compositionally similar to human plasma.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Human plasma is actually a light amber colour! And if you mean deoxygenated blood, it only really ever gets to a dark maroon colour. The cells of veins appear blue because they are, but the blood within is still primarily red. <a href="https://cdn.arstechnica.net/wp-content/uploads/2016/10/NIK_3232-Drops_of_blood_medium.jpg">Here's a visual example; the darker sample is deoxygenated.</a></p>
<p>I also personally prefer footnotes to be placed after punctuation.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-723347-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-723347-1')">1</a></sup></p>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">I&nbsp;have&nbsp;hawk&nbsp;eyes&nbsp;for&nbsp;weird&nbsp;phrasing&nbsp;and&nbsp;science</a></div>
</div>
</div>
<p>edit: accidental footnote removed :p</p>
<p>Overall: I <em>love</em> biology horror. I think the actual biology-related stuff could use some tightening up in general. Bio is one of my best subjects for science though, so might not be fair to those not great at it, so if the simplification is keeping the learning curve down, that's fine.</p>
<p>+1!</p>
